Subject: [PATCH 24/28] Arp roll / bounce length: review fixes (hung note,
 silent spans, swing, sequence length)

- Unsynced (or synced with the transport stopped), a ratchet lasting several steps always moves
  on into its next step, and a step that is over always ends its note and starts the next one,
  whatever the gate. Before, replacing latched notes or a forced arp restart mid-ratchet could
  stop the arp with its note hanging (1 note-on and no note-off in 4 bars, in the emulator).
- A ratchet only lasts several steps if the step's note plays: a note left out by the note
  probability is a one-step rest, as before, not a rest over the whole bounce length.
- A ratchet never lasts past the end of the sequence length, so the arp starts over on time.
- Synced, inside a ratchet lasting several steps, its position doesn't run into the next step
  before the clock's tick (swing, an external clock), and hits of the last step that the tick
  left unplayed are dropped (as a new step drops what's left of its ratchet), except one due just
  before the tick that doesn't run into the next: no more double hits 128 samples apart with swing.
- Menu: isRelevant back in the public part of RatchetNotes.

In the emulator (real firmware): the 11 edge cases of the review pass (latch unsynced with length
1/4 and a roll, synced latch, sequence length, note probability, swing, release and press again);
the 7 roll/bounce cases give exactly the same hits as before; the full-load song renders
bit-identical.

